sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User Browser
    participant KRP as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant JL as JupyterLab<br/>8888/TCP HTTP
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Nginx as nginx<br/>8888/TCP HTTP
    participant CGI as httpd CGI<br/>8080/TCP HTTP
    participant CS as code-server<br/>8787/TCP HTTP
    participant Culler as Notebook Controller<br/>Culler
    participant Elyra as Elyra Pipeline Editor
    participant DSPA as DSPA Endpoint<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Runtime as Runtime Image Pod

    Note over User, JL: Flow 1: Workbench Launch (Jupyter)
    User->>KRP: HTTPS/8443<br/>OpenShift OAuth
    KRP->>JL: HTTP/8888<br/>(pod-internal, no auth)
    JL->>K8s: HTTPS/443<br/>ServiceAccount Token
    K8s-->>JL: API Response
    JL-->>KRP: HTTP Response
    KRP-->>User: HTTPS Response

    Note over Culler, CS: Flow 2: Code-Server Idle Culling
    Culler->>KRP: HTTPS/8443<br/>ServiceAccount Token
    KRP->>Nginx: HTTP/8888<br/>(pod-internal)
    Nginx->>CGI: HTTP/8080<br/>GET /api/kernels/
    CGI->>CS: HTTP/8787<br/>GET /healthz (localhost)
    CS-->>CGI: Healthz Response
    CGI-->>Nginx: Jupyter-compatible<br/>kernels JSON
    Nginx-->>KRP: Response
    KRP-->>Culler: HTTPS Response

    Note over User, Runtime: Flow 3: Elyra Pipeline Execution
    User->>JL: Opens pipeline editor
    JL->>Elyra: Pipeline definition
    Elyra->>DSPA: HTTPS/443<br/>Bearer Token<br/>(from mounted DSPA secret)
    DSPA->>K8s: HTTPS/443<br/>Create pipeline run<br/>ServiceAccount Token
    K8s->>Runtime: Launches runtime pod
    Runtime->>Runtime: Elyra bootstrapper.py<br/>executes notebook cells
    Runtime-->>DSPA: Pipeline step complete
    DSPA-->>Elyra: Pipeline status
